Z||000000||phillip||04-21-2000||01:08 PM||||<BR> kinda off the wall idea. i have the '87-'88 coupe/formula front end. what if i could cut the front bumper right at the leading edge wheel to wheel. find an identical bumper cut it the same way, turn it upside down and graft it (glass, rivets, whatever it takes)to mine to lower the front spoiler. <P>i guess it wouldn't be quite that simple but hopefully you get the idea? dose it sound doable? any body folks have an opinion? any computer graphics types want to try to look at it. my plates kind of full money and time wise right now but i keep looking at it and if i don't get some strong negative feedback (and don't encourage me just to see if "that fool will destroy his car") i'll start looking for another bumper to cut up.  <P>or i guess the best thing would be to try to get two more bumpers and leave mine alone until i get it right. <P>somebody stop me.||||reg||1
